TITLE:: ReverbView
summary:: the reverbs' display: the frame each one draws its own space in
categories:: Libraries>Reverbs
related:: Classes/HallView, Classes/PlateView, Classes/CoilView, Classes/ShimmerView, Classes/FxParamView, Classes/FxDevicePanel

DESCRIPTION::
What link::Classes/FxDevicePanel:: puts at the top of the window of a reverb. Time runs along, a strip at the top reads out the settings, and each reverb draws its own kind of space on it, worked out from its settings (not measured):

table::
## link::Classes/HallView:: || the onset - the gap, the walls, the slow swell - beside the long fall
## link::Classes/PlateView:: || a sheet, dense from the first moment, held flat by hold
## link::Classes/CoilView:: || a lane per spring, each round trip a chirp, smearing as it goes
## link::Classes/ShimmerView:: || pitch against time: each round an interval higher, fading
::

Behind the drawing, in signal blue, is the output itself: after each hit (the input jumping 9 dB over where it was) the out meter's readings are drawn from the moment of the hit, so a sound rings out along the slope the settings say. It needs the meter replies a window turns on; with no hit it starts again whenever the sweep runs off the display.

This class alone draws a plain tail (a gap for the pre-delay, the fall to 60 dB down, the highs at 5 kHz falling sooner) for any link::Classes/FxParamUnit:: that names its decay, pre-delay and damping in code::*viewKeys::.

subsection:: Mouse

table::
## drag a handle || what the hint bar says it moves; shift: a tenth as fast
## drag anywhere else || along: the decay; up and down: the damping (each face may say otherwise)
## double click || a handle's parameters back to their defaults (anywhere else: what a drag there moves)
## the wheel || the face's second hero: the size, the drip, the feedback
::

Hover over a handle and it grows, and the hint bar names it.

subsection:: Writing a face
A subclass writes code::prCompute:: (an Event of what it draws, worked out again only when a setting or the size changes, its code::\handles:: among it: Events with code::at::, a Point, code::x:: and/or code::y::, the parameters a drag along and up moves, and a code::hint::), code::prDrawFace:: and code::caption::; code::prFreeKeys::, code::prWheelKey:: and code::prFreeHint:: say what the rest of the display does.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: unit
One of the reverbs.
ARGUMENT:: parent
A view to go in.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: hint
What the hint bar says with the pointer at x, y: the handle under it, or what dragging there does.
ARGUMENT:: x
In the view's coordinates.
ARGUMENT:: y
In the view's coordinates.

METHOD:: caption
The readout along the top.

METHOD:: captionRight
What the readout says at its right, in the reverb's colour, or nil (a held plate, a runaway shimmer).

METHOD:: levelsArrived
Called by the panel on every meter reply: adds the out level to the sweep, or starts a new one on a hit.

METHOD:: sweep
The readings drawn now, as code::[seconds since the hit, dB]:: pairs.

METHOD:: sweepTop
The loudest of them, in dB.

METHOD:: sweepHit
Whether a hit started the sweep (false when it started because the last one ran off the display).

METHOD:: model
What the face drew last: the Event code::prCompute:: answered.

EXAMPLES::

code::
h = Hall.new;
h.gui;
h.decay = 6;	// the tail's end moves out
::
